<title>JAPAN: Mitsui says buys 7,400 tonnes of corn from China.</title>
<headline>Mitsui says buys 7,400 tonnes of corn from China.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Mitsui &amp; Co Ltd said on Wednesday that it bought 7,400 tonnes of feed corn from China for May and July shipment.  </p>
<p>China suspended corn exports in late 1994 due to rising domestic grain prices and accelerating inflation. Before that China was one of Japan's top corn suppliers, along with the United States. Corn is used in Japan to make feed.</p>
<p>--Eiichiro Tokumoto, Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
